4. TABLE: blogs
========================================================

    CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS blogs (
        id             UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
        name           VARCHAR(15) NOT NULL,
        description    VARCHAR(500) NOT NULL,
        website_url    VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
        is_membership  BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE,
        created_at     TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
        updated_at     TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
        deleted_at     TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NULL
    );

Columns:
  - id (UUID, PK)            — Auto-generated primary key.
  - name (VARCHAR(15))       — Blog name. Max 15 characters (matches validation rules).
  - description (VARCHAR(500))— Blog description.
  - website_url (VARCHAR(100))— Blog's external website URL.
  - is_membership (BOOLEAN)  — Whether the blog requires membership. Defaults to FALSE.
  - created_at, updated_at, deleted_at — Standard audit and soft delete columns.

Indexes:
  No additional indexes beyond the primary key. The blogs table is relatively small
  and typically accessed by ID. Listing queries use sequential scan with pagination.

Trigger:
  Same BEFORE UPDATE trigger pattern for auto-updating updated_at.

Design decisions:
  - Simple table with no foreign keys — blogs are top-level entities.
  - VARCHAR lengths match the application-level validation constraints (e.g.,
    name max 15 chars matches the class-validator @MaxLength(15) on input DTOs).


